  "section_notes": "The final text sets a 7% permanent model limit in S2 with no automatic sales stop, which protects the Hearth 10 (6.2%), while the 5% line only triggers regulator review. S5 makes recall discretionary rather than mandatory at 8 per 100,000, which protects the Ember 8 (9.9). S1 reporting (24h for confirmed incidents) is stricter than the answer key requires, and S4's 36-month suppression start matches Halcyon's red line. The S5 permanent_trigger is recorded as null because the 8/100k figure only triggers review, not a mandatory recall."
